2. External tools and datasets used at run time (not bundled)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

scrcpy (https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy) ........ Apache License 2.0
  Started as a separate program. Agentroid builds its command line and parses
  its output; no scrcpy source or binary is included.

AndroidWorld (https://github.com/google-research/android_world) .. Apache-2.0
  The benchmark harness for the scripts in bench/androidworld. It is installed
  separately and imported, not vendored. bench/androidworld/action_map.py
  re-implements the semantics of android_world's execute_adb_action from
  reading it, with no copied code.

UI Automator (Android Open Source Project) .......... Apache License 2.0
  The platform's own "uiautomator dump" command is called through adb. When
  that command cannot read a screen that never goes idle, bridged runs its
  fallback reader, crates/bridged/assets/idle-free-dump/Dump.java (and the dex
  built from it). The reader calls the device's own
  /system/framework/uiautomator.jar by reflection, in the same order as AOSP's
  DumpCommand (platform/frameworks/testing, uiautomator/cmds/uiautomator), with
  a shorter idle wait. The call order follows that file; no source lines are
  copied, and the file's header says so. Neither the jar nor any UI Automator
  binary is included.

